jobs.description:
Deltamed’s mission
is to produce special-purpose vehicles of the highest quality, providing confidence and safety in critical situations. To meet the real needs of our customers, we continuously invest in advanced production technologies, modern materials and equipment, and in the ongoing development of our people.
https://www.deltamed.ro/

In this role, you will coordinate technical projects for special vehicles and customized solutions
, from initiation to final delivery. You will work closely with engineering, production, procurement and management teams
to ensure projects are delivered on time, within budget and according to technical and contractual requirements.

This is a hands-on technical project management role
, close to the product and manufacturing environment, with direct impact on customer satisfaction and project performance.

MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES:

What you will do

Manage technical projects for the production and outfitting of special vehicles and customized solutions from initiation to final acceptance;
Develop detailed project plans, define milestones and ensure effective allocation of internal resources;
Lead cross-functional teams (design, production, procurement, logistics, quality) to achieve project objectives;
Monitor project progress, organize regular meetings and implement corrective actions when deviations occur;
Manage communication with internal and external stakeholders and maintain alignment regarding scope, deadlines, costs and technical expectations;
Track project budgets, costs, contracts and resource utilization throughout the project lifecycle;
Identify technical and operational risks and propose alternative solutions;
Ensure project documentation is complete and up to date and report project status to management;
Participate in final project deliveries and customer acceptance activities;
Apply lessons learned principles and contribute to continuous improvement of future projects and processes.

What a typical day in this role could look like

Review project status, deadlines and resource planning;
Coordinate a technical meeting with engineering and production teams regarding an ongoing vehicle build;
Analyze project risks, supplier constraints or technical changes;
Update project plans, budgets and documentation in ERP and project management systems;
Prepare a progress report for management and define corrective actions;
Participate in customer or partner technical discussions.

REQUIREMENTS:

University degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Machine Building or a related technical field;
Minimum 5 years of experience in a technical environment such as automotive, machine building, manufacturing or engineering;
Minimum 5 years of experience in project management; international project experience is an advantage;
Proven experience managing projects through the full lifecycle, from planning to delivery;
Solid understanding of manufacturing processes, engineering technologies, budgeting and contract management;
Experience with project management tools such as OpenProject, Jira, Teamcenter or similar;
Experience working with ERP systems for planning, BOM management, manufacturing tracking and project monitoring;
German language – fluent ;the role involves regular spoken and written communication with German-speaking customers, suppliers and partners;
English language – at least intermediate level, both written and spoken, including technical terminology;
Driving licence category B;
Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills;
Analytical thinking, organizational skills and results orientation;
Genuine interest in engineering, technology and continuous improvement.

It would be an advantage if you already have experience in

Special vehicles, automotive, railway, military or other complex manufacturing industries;
International customer projects and multicultural project teams;
System integration and customized technical solutions;
Operational optimization and continuous improvement projects;
Collaboration with executive management and senior stakeholders.

Why Deltamed?

At Deltamed, you will work on projects that become real vehicles used in emergency and critical operations. Your work will have a visible impact on the quality, functionality and successful delivery of complex technical products.
You will be part of a collaborative engineering environment where technical expertise, initiative and continuous improvement are valued, and where project managers play an active role in shaping both products and processes.

Standard benefits

Meal tickets worth 35 RON/day worked;
Bonuses and special occasion benefits;
23 vacation days/year;
1 paid day off on your birthday;
Additional vacation days based on seniority within the company;
Company transportation to and from the workplace;
Modern working environment with safe and comfortable working conditions;
Professional development opportunities through internal and external training programs;
Internal work-from-home program – 1 day/month.

If you are passionate about manufacturing engineering and want to contribute to products that make a real difference, we would be happy to hear from you.

Candidates who possess the qualifications and are able to demonstrate their ability to meet the specific requirements of the role are well-positioned to succeed.

All applications will be treated confidentially. Only candidates selected based on the initial evaluation will be contacted for the next stages of the selection process. Our company promotes equal opportunities and conducts selection based on skills, professional fit, and aptitude assessments.

📍 Location:
Gilău, Cluj County, Romania, on-site job
📩 Apply directly via LinkedIn
or send your CV to our recruitment team at cariere@deltamed.ro

